      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "I believe this was back before the udon networking update, which introduced manual sync. Continuous sync still has this limitation and it is not a bug, continuous sync is simply limited to about 256 bytes. Manual sync on the other hand allows up to around 60 thousand bytes, so I'm going to consider this complete.",
